---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Clean Slate"
  description="How Clean Slate Professional Clean Up Services collects, uses, and protects information when you visit our website or request our services."
>

  <Header />

  <main>

    <section>
      <div class="container max-w-3xl">

        <h1 class="mt-12 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mb-10 text-sm text-muted">Last Updated: August 31, 2026</p>

        <div class="legal-prose text-body">

          <p>
            Clean Slate Professional Clean Up Services (&ldquo;Clean Slate,&rdquo;
            &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) respects
            your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and
            protect information when you visit our website or request or purchase
            our services.
          </p>

          <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>We may collect information you voluntarily provide, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Name</li>
            <li>Phone number</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Service address</li>
            <li>Billing or payment information</li>
            <li>Information about items or services requested</li>
            <li>Photos submitted through our booking process</li>
            <li>Scheduling information</li>
            <li>Messages and other communications with us</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We may also automatically collect limited technical information such
            as IP address, browser type, device information, pages visited, and
            general website usage information.
          </p>

          <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
          <p>We may use information we collect to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Provide and schedule services</li>
            <li>Calculate or confirm pricing</li>
            <li>Communicate with customers</li>
            <li>Process payments</li>
            <li>Respond to questions and service requests</li>
            <li>Improve our website and services</li>
            <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, or security issues</li>
            <li>Maintain business and transaction records</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>3. Photos and Customer-Submitted Content</h2>
          <p>
            Photos and other information submitted through our booking system may
            be used to evaluate the requested service, determine pricing, prepare
            our crew, and communicate about the job.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not sell customer-submitted photos or personal information.
          </p>

          <h2>4. Payments</h2>
          <p>
            Payments may be processed through third-party payment providers.
            Clean Slate does not need to store your complete credit card number
            to process payments.
          </p>
          <p>
            Payment information may be handled directly by the applicable payment
            provider and is subject to that provider&rsquo;s privacy practices.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Service Providers</h2>
          <p>
            We may use third-party companies to provide website hosting,
            scheduling, payment processing, analytics, communications, maps, and
            other business services.
          </p>
          <p>
            These providers may process information on our behalf as necessary to
            provide their services.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            Our website may use cookies, analytics tools, or similar technologies
            to understand website usage, improve performance, and measure
            marketing effectiveness.
          </p>
          <p>
            You may be able to control certain cookies through your browser
            settings.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Communications</h2>
          <p>
            If you provide your phone number or email address, we may use it to
            communicate with you regarding requested services, appointments,
            payments, and other customer-service matters.
          </p>
          <p>
            We may also send promotional communications where permitted by law.
            You can request to stop receiving promotional communications at any
            time.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Information Sharing</h2>
          <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information.</p>
          <p>
            We may share information with service providers, payment processors,
            technology providers, contractors, or other parties when reasonably
            necessary to provide our services, operate our business, protect our
            rights, prevent fraud, or comply with legal requirements.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
          <p>
            We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational
            measures to protect information. However, no website, transmission,
            or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We may retain customer information for as long as reasonably
            necessary to provide services, maintain business records, resolve
            disputes, comply with legal obligations, and fulfill other legitimate
            business purposes.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our website and services are not directed toward children under 13.
            We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under
            13.
          </p>

          <h2>12. External Websites</h2>
          <p>
            Our website may contain links to third-party websites or services. We
            are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of those
            third parties.
          </p>

          <h2>13. Your Privacy Choices</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on applicable law, you may have rights regarding your
            personal information, including requesting access, correction, or
            deletion of certain information.
          </p>
          <p>
            To make a privacy-related request, contact Clean Slate using the
            contact information provided on our website.
          </p>

          <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be
            posted on this page with an updated &ldquo;Last Updated&rdquo; date.
          </p>

          <h2>15. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how Clean Slate
            handles your information, please contact us through the contact
            information provided on our website.
          </p>

          <p>
            By using our website, you acknowledge that you have had the
            opportunity to review this Privacy Policy.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--heading);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-prose ul {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .legal-prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
